<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12121" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cylindrus</span></b> , dri,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύλινδρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a cylinder</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 10, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fat. 19,
			41</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A cylindrical stone for levelling the ground, a
				roller</i>, etc., <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			129</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1, 178</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 19,
				8, 46, § 158</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10,
				6 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A precious stone ground off in the form of a
				cylinder</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 5, 20, § 78</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">37, 8, 34, §
				113</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 2, 61 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>